WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.014
In under two minutes, you will share your contest with your neighbors.

00:00:04.014 --> 00:00:05.033
We start on the map.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:09.266
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:13.512
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:16.001
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.001 --> 00:00:17.347
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.094 --> 00:00:21.310
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:21.962
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.468 --> 00:00:27.963
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:27.963 --> 00:00:29.181
See the three dots?

00:00:29.181 --> 00:00:29.729
Tap them.

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:33.296
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:35.622
Tap Mine.

00:00:35.622 --> 00:00:37.570
These are the contests you run.

00:00:39.251 --> 00:00:41.273
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:41.273 --> 00:00:42.641
This is your dashboard.

00:00:44.525 --> 00:00:47.381
On the Overview, find the card called Share it.

00:00:48.562 --> 00:00:53.787
Tap Copy link, then paste it into an email, a text, or a Facebook post.

00:00:55.519 --> 00:00:59.574
The QR code opens your contest when someone scans it with a phone.

00:00:59.574 --> 00:01:01.208
Put it on flyers and signs.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:05.174
Print entry poster makes a page for a bulletin board.

00:01:05.174 --> 00:01:06.139
Here is a sample.

00:01:08.356 --> 00:01:10.985
Print yard sign makes a big sign for a lawn.

00:01:10.985 --> 00:01:11.979
Here is a sample.

00:01:14.295 --> 00:01:17.093
To invite neighbors by email, tap Promote.

00:01:19.306 --> 00:01:21.272
Open Invite neighbors by email.

00:01:21.272 --> 00:01:23.544
Type their addresses, and add a note.

00:01:25.222 --> 00:01:29.588
Each neighbor gets an invitation like this one, with your note and one button.

00:01:30.588 --> 00:01:33.514
Next up: Approve and decline entries.
